    doc = '# X50: fyndvis bettscreening mot klinikerrapporter\n\n' + lead + _release_expand("\n\nThe idea is that each finding needs its own sensitivity at the given false alarm level.21 are linked to the recorded arcs and the explicit category or region of reports. Anterior opening and lateral opening are preserved separately before the consumer takes the Union.\n\nRun `./run_all.sh`Requires Python3, NumPy, SciPy, scikit-learn and existing X7 vendor_plotting for NumPy2-compatible matplotlib; no download or replay model change. For one case: `python3 code/demo_case.py --case @DENTAL_CASE_ID@ --round R3 --specificity 0.95 --out raw/DEMO_CASE.json`. JSON exports seven explicitly defined research flags: six original findings and R4's coverage of all regions, with tooth-pair sources and a population gate. A score is not a calibrated individual diagnostic probability.\n\n") + '\n'.join(table) + "\n\nThe table is a **beskrivande, icke-randomiserad test-ROC**: the threshold is chosen with the test reference and re-selected in each of the following: 2000 stratified patient-boot stairways. It is not a use threshold for a new case. Threshold selection and data resolution make actual specificity sometimes higher than the target. All numbers are shares; 95%-intervall avser POPULATION over PER_ARCH-fall. New all-region open bite has 21 positive test cases; previous anterior trials had 15 and is unchanged.\n\nThe thresholds actually used by a new case were selected on separate calibration cases before the round's test comparison:\n\n" + '\n'.join(deploy) + "\n\nIngen fryst screeninggrind passerar. Krav: minst 20 positiva/30 negative, actual test-Sp at least target and lower sensitivity-Wilson at least 0,80. No confidence guarantee that the specificity of the new centre is maintained 0,90 eller 0,95 available. Anterior opening (R2) captured 15/15, Wilson [0,796,1,000]; it was too few positive. (R4) Prisoners 18/21 vid Sp0,931 and 17/21 vid Sp0,948. This makes the wider user question more difficult, not validated by 15/15-talet.\n\n[Figure: screening and threshold transfer](figures/screening_sensitivity.png). [Figure: Changed range](figures/scope_extension.png). [Felfall som meshbilder](figures/error_cases.png). Alla fel, inklusive samtliga FN/FP, lies in raw/ERRORS_R1.json till raw/ERRORS_R4.json.\n\n" + '\n'.join(noise) + "\n\nDouble report files are observation pairs with unknown author and repeat identity.(rapport2+|rapport1+) from P(rapport2−|rapport1−). En total 7–16%-disunity does not identify any sensitivity floor. For each finding is **an inter/intra-assessing noise floor UNKNOWN**. The reports can contribute with observation consistency, but scope, translation, omission, parses and assessor errors are not separated. posterior/allregionopening is only available 14 rapport1-positive double reported test cases; no safely measured noise limit follows. Intra-assess variation is not identified.\n\nPatient sharing is X7:s 593 training /198 kalibrering /198 test without ID-overlap. Casefolder as patient identity is supported by the dataset primary page. These test cases have previously been seen in X7/X21/X39 and before later X50-constructions: this is a testable descriptive replay, not a new patient validation. No test parameter adjustment is made within the respective frozen construction.\n\nThree adequacy tests have been carried out: **identitetsfel exakt 0** i binary64. Samma totalnoggrannhet 0,90 may have sensitivity 0 eller 1; samma total rapportoenighet 0,10 may have positive compliance 0,80 eller 1; samma medianmarginal 2 mm may have or lack a local negative margin. Minimal extensions: a class-conditional confusion matrix, positiva/negativa report compliances; and minimum/per-tand Signed Margin. These are custom mathematical counter-examples, not clinical reference observations. No affinity physical sensitivity or rigorous physical uncertainty inclusion is reported.\n\nDen starka konventionella HGB-control is actually refitted with the same information and provides exactly the same scores; logistic regression on the same regional data is presented separately in results.json. Control does not establish any algorithm news. Clinical practice without the patient's bite data is not measured; all-negative gives sensitivity0/Sp1 and random order provides expected 1−Sp as purely mathematical comparisons.\n\nWhat doesn't hold: target-FDI and named cusp/groove are independent unvalidated; 877/993 source poses had according to X21 Projected overlap>0,03 Closeness/overlapping is therefore not a physical contact force. Saxbetet's positive reference observations include insecure/”almost”- statements; silence is UNKNOWN, giving 106/198 The report's negative overbited category without a positive lateral clause is a full report, not proven lateral absence. Genuine assessor noise and external clinical practice advantage lacks reference sightings.\n\nLicens: Bite2Text-villkor UNKNOWN efter lokal ZIP- and primary side control; private local research, no raw publishing. Bits2Bites CC BY-NC-SA according to briefen, only archive metadata was inspected and no data is used in the models. ToothFairy2/mandibeldefekter/MMDental not used. X21:s target segmentation is reused; the model was trained on Teeth3DS med delvis oklar lokal snapshotlicens, se X21:s manifest. Inga personfoton, namn eller journaluppgifter exporteras. Bara avidentifierade dataset-ID and clinical findings.\n\nCost includes reuse: X7:s geometri 1254,26 s and X21:s kartbyggande 681,91 s, plus deras fit/segmentering and subsequent checks in: COSTS.json. New fit, validation, question time and replay are measured separately; a failed R2-progressprint gav en extra omfit med separat tid UNKNOWN. Source search/development cost and physical assessment UNKNOWNNo speed gain is claimed. Arrayer/modeller on the data disk with: SHA256; lane boundary3GB, ≤2 threads, none GPU.\n\nNext necessary measurement: locked blind region/tandwise assessment of named assessors on new patients, two re-assessments and repeated bite registration; see MEASUREMENT_SPEC.md and FROZEN_MEASUREMENT_PANEL.json. Status PENDING_INDEPENDENT_REVIEW.\n"
    open_pairs = rounds['R4']['methods']['candidate']['0.9']['report_noise_context']['report_pair']['npos']
